# GRADUATED FROM `known_gaps/` in Round XXIII (γδ 2026-08-01) — closed
# by the `infer_collection_element_type` class fix (adds `Deque__` arm)
# + kind-gate admitting `Map`.
#
# CORE #11/#12 REGRESSION — `&d[i].fd` write-through on struct-payload
# Deque + single-evaluation of the index.
#
# AXIS PIN: Deque[S] struct payload · `&d[idx()].fd` call-arg amp ·
# elem-type `Deque__S` → resolved via `infer_collection_element_type`
# (methods.rs). Kind-gate at `try_resolve_index_element_ptr` already
# admitted Deque via `CollectionKind::Array` (builtins.rs).
#
# RED-VERIFIED PRE-FIX (Round XXIII γ scout 2026-08-01):
#   - C: SIGSEGV, exit 139, no output (cc1 warned
#     `expected 'void *' but argument is of type 'int32_t'`).
#   - LLVM: NO BINARY — `llc` hard-fails
#     `'%v22' defined with type 'i32' but expected 'ptr'`.
# Same shape both backends. Post-fix both lanes produce a binary and
# print `IDX / 11` — the LLVM-lane caveat that the earlier known_gaps
# header carried is dropped.
#
# The `IDX`-once half also pins the reachable emit-then-`None` row:
# pre-fix the resolver emitted the collection lowering, the index
# lowering AND the `index_load` BEFORE returning `None`, then the
# caller re-lowered the base — visible on the assign-face twin as
# `d[idx()].fd = 7` printing `IDX/IDX/0`. The assign-face DOUBLE-EVAL
# is a separate Family-1 disposition (see TODO.md) and is NOT closed
# by this fix.
from std.collections import Deque

struct S:
    int fd

int idx():
    print("IDX")
    return 0

void inc(int &n):
    n = n + 1

void main():
    Deque[S] d = Deque[S]()
    d.push(S(10))
    inc(&d[idx()].fd)
    print(d[0].fd)
